<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLAND BUILD BIG FIRST INNINGS LEAD.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLAND BUILD BIG FIRST INNINGS LEAD.</headline>
<dateline>PALMERSTON NORTH, New Zealand 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New Zealand Selection XI trailed England by 264 runs with nine second innings wickets standing at the close of the third day's play in their four-day tour match on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Scores:</p>
<p>New Zealand Selection XI 138 and 25-1</p>
<p>England 427-8 declared (A. Stewart 153 retired hurt, N. Hussain 139)</p>
